# =========================
# .antigravityrules (v1.2)
# React ATC Control Center Frontend Standard (Backend: Spring Boot / Java 17)
# SSOT: Single Source of Truth for frontend conventions.
# =========================

[0. ABSOLUTE PRIORITY: LEGACY-LOCK RULE (NON-BREAKING ONLY)]
0.1 MUST NOT delete or modify existing features, behaviors, outputs, UI flows, routes, event schemas, side-effects, or public contracts.
0.2 All changes MUST be additive by default:
    - Add new files, new components, new routes, new fields, new handlers, new adapters.
    - Do NOT alter existing logic paths or outputs.
0.3 Bug fixes MUST follow the same additive protocol:
    - Keep old behavior intact.
    - Introduce fixed behavior behind a feature flag or new code path.
    - Default remains old behavior unless explicitly enabled.
0.4 Non-breaking Change Protocol (MANDATORY):
    A) Preserve old behavior (tests must keep passing).
    B) Add new behavior behind a feature flag OR a new contract version (route/key/eventType).
    C) Add compatibility adapter if needed (new ↔ old).
    D) Mark old behavior as DEPRECATED (comment + doc), but keep it working.
    E) Provide migration plan + tests proving old behavior still passes.
0.5 Breaking changes allowed ONLY if ALL satisfied:
    - Approved by 2 reviewers (one must be “contract owner”)
    - Changelog entry
    - Migration guide + compatibility window (date/version)
    - Regression tests verifying old contract behavior until sunset
0.6 Public contract stability MUST be enforced:
    - API DTO shape, response wrapper, error codes, query params, localStorage keys, route params, MQTT/WS event payloads.
    - Contract evolution: ONLY add optional fields or add new versions. NEVER rename/remove existing fields.

[1. STACK: FIXED DEFAULTS (NO PERSONAL TASTE ALLOWED)]
1.1 MUST use:
    - Node: LTS only
    - Package manager: pnpm only
    - Build: Vite
    - Language: TypeScript (strict)
    - Lint/Format: ESLint + Prettier
    - Git hooks: Husky + lint-staged
    - Testing: Vitest + React Testing Library
1.2 Styling MUST use: Tailwind CSS
1.3 UI primitives MUST use: shadcn/ui pattern (project-owned components). No other UI kit.
1.4 Server state MUST use: TanStack Query
1.5 Global app state MUST use: Zustand (only truly global, not everything)
1.6 Routing MUST use: TanStack Router (do NOT mix React Router)
1.7 Runtime validation MUST use: Zod at boundaries (API + realtime)
1.8 Date handling MUST use: dayjs (single lib). No native Date formatting in UI.

[2. TYPESCRIPT + CONFIG: STRICT BY DEFAULT]
2.1 TypeScript MUST be strict:
    - strict: true
    - noImplicitAny: true
    - exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true (preferred)
    - noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true (preferred)
2.2 MUST NOT use `any` (ban). Allowed only with explicit justification:
    - `// EXCEPTION(any): reason, owner, removal-date`
2.3 Prefer `unknown` + Zod parse instead of `any`.
2.4 Path aliases:
    - MUST use "@/..." mapped to "src/..."
    - No deep relative imports "../../.."

[3. PROJECT STRUCTURE: FIXED]
3.1 Root structure (MUST follow):
- src/
  - app/                # bootstrap: providers, router, query client, theme, flags
  - pages/              # route-level UI (thin: layout + composition only)
  - features/           # user flows (approve mission, manual mode, etc.)
  - entities/           # domain models (aircraft, towcar, mission, alert)
  - widgets/            # large reusable blocks (map panel, alert feed, inspector)
  - shared/
      - ui/             # base UI components + shadcn overrides
      - api/            # api client + dto + schemas + adapters
      - realtime/       # ws/mqtt clients + schemas + adapters
      - lib/            # pure utils (format, math, guards)
      - config/         # env, constants, endpoints, feature flags registry
      - hooks/          # reusable hooks (not domain-specific)
  - assets/
  - styles/
  - tests/              # msw, fixtures, contract snapshots

3.2 Placement rules:
- Domain object model/state: src/entities/<domain>/
- Flow composition: src/features/<flow>/
- Complex block used across pages: src/widgets/<widget>/
- Reusable UI atoms: src/shared/ui/
- External boundary logic: src/shared/api/, src/shared/realtime/

3.3 Barrel exports:
- Allowed only at module boundary index.ts
- MUST NOT cause circular deps
- Export only public surface

[4. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (VITE RULES)]
4.1 All client env vars MUST start with: VITE_
4.2 Required env keys (MUST define):
    - VITE_API_BASE_URL
    - VITE_WS_BASE_URL (if WS used)
    - VITE_MQTT_BROKER_URL (if mqtt over ws)
    - VITE_FEATURE_FLAGS (optional json string or empty)
4.3 No secrets in frontend env (API keys/tokens must not be embedded).
4.4 Env access must be centralized in src/shared/config/env.ts (single gate).

[5. NAMING CONVENTIONS: STRICT]
5.1 folders: kebab-case
5.2 component files: PascalCase.tsx
5.3 hooks: useCamelCase.ts
5.4 utilities: camelCase.ts
5.5 schemas: *.schema.ts (Zod)
5.6 types: *.types.ts (or colocated, but consistent per module)
5.7 tests: *.test.ts / *.test.tsx
5.8 Identifiers:
- Components: PascalCase
- Functions/vars: camelCase
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Booleans: is/has/can/should/was/will prefix
5.9 Handlers:
- Props callbacks: onX
- Internal handlers: handleX
5.10 Prohibited names:
- any, foo, bar, tmp, data1, test123, thing

[6. REACT CODING RULES]
6.1 Function components only.
6.2 Props typing:
- Use `type` by default, `interface` only when extension is necessary.
6.3 Component file order:
- imports → types → constants → component → helpers
6.4 State rules:
- No derived state unless proven necessary.
- Server state: TanStack Query only.
- UI global state: Zustand only.
6.5 Effects:
- useEffect MUST NOT fetch data (use Query).
- Allowed for subscriptions, imperative bridges (map engine), external sync.
6.6 Accessibility:
- No clickable divs. Use button/a.
- Inputs must have label or aria-label.
6.7 Performance:
- No blanket memoization.
- Stable keys: id only (no index keys when reorder possible).
6.8 Logging:
- No console.log in committed code.
- console.error allowed only in error boundary or DEV-gated diagnostics.
6.9 Error boundaries:
- App root MUST have ErrorBoundary with safe fallback UI.

[7. STYLE SYSTEM (TAILWIND + DESIGN TOKENS)]
7.1 Tailwind only. No styled-components/emotion/sass.
7.2 Inline style allowed only for dynamic transforms/positions not expressible cleanly.
7.3 Design tokens:
- Use CSS variables + tailwind config mapping.
- Theme (dark ops) must be via tokens, not ad-hoc hex codes.
7.4 Shared components live in src/shared/ui/ and must not be duplicated.

[8. API + CONTRACTS (SPRING BOOT / JAVA 17 FIT)]
8.1 Single API client:
- src/shared/api/client.ts is the only place that touches fetch/axios.
8.2 DTO boundary:
- All API responses MUST be validated with Zod schemas at boundary.
- DTO types in src/shared/api/dto/
- Domain models in src/entities/<domain>/model/
- Adapters dtoToDomain live near domain.
8.3 Response wrapper standard (FRONTEND EXPECTATION):
- If backend uses envelope like { success, data, error }, parse and normalize.
- Normalize ALL errors into:
  { code: string; message: string; detail?: unknown; retryable?: boolean }
8.4 Date/time contract:
- Treat backend timestamps as ISO-8601 strings.
- UI formatting via dayjs only.
8.5 Pagination contract:
- If backend returns page info, adapter must map into a single internal shape:
  { items: T[]; page: number; size: number; total?: number; hasNext?: boolean }
8.6 Auth contract:
- Token storage keys are public contracts (do not rename).
- Token handling must be centralized (no scattered localStorage access).

[9. REALTIME (WS/MQTT) RULES]
9.1 Single ingress layer:
- All WS/MQTT clients live in src/shared/realtime/
- Components MUST NOT subscribe directly.
9.2 Message validation:
- Every event payload MUST have Zod schema.
- Invalid messages MUST be dropped safely with DEV diagnostics (no crash).
9.3 Store update:
- Realtime updates Zustand through actions only.
9.4 Buffering:
- Default: latest snapshot only.
- History requires bounded buffer (max size/time).
9.5 Contract stability:
- Topic names, event types, payload fields are public contracts (see [0]).

[10. FEATURE FLAGS (MANDATORY FOR CHANGES)]
10.1 Feature flags registry must exist:
- src/shared/config/flags.ts
10.2 Any new behavior that might replace old behavior MUST be behind a flag.
10.3 Flags are the only allowed mechanism to ship “new without breaking old”.

[11. QUALITY GATES]
11.1 Pre-commit (lint-staged) MUST run:
- eslint, prettier, typecheck (affected)
11.2 CI MUST run:
- pnpm lint
- pnpm typecheck
- pnpm test
- pnpm build
11.3 PR approvals:
- Normal: >=1 approval
- Contract areas (shared/api, shared/realtime, router, entities models): >=2 approvals
11.4 Tests:
- New feature must include unit + critical UI test when applicable.
- Any change must prove old behavior remains (regression test or contract snapshot).

[12. CODE STYLE DETAILS]
12.1 Import order MUST be enforced (eslint):
- react/vendor → internal (@/...) → relative → styles
12.2 No unused exports, no implicit side-effect imports.
12.3 No default exports except route components (optional). Prefer named exports.

[13. GIT + COMMITS]
13.1 Conventional Commits required:
- feat:, fix:, chore:, refactor:, docs:, test:
13.2 Branching:
- main (release), dev (integration), feature/<ticket>-<short>
13.3 No force push to main/dev.
13.4 Any contract impact requires changelog entry.

[14. ANTI-LEGACY DECLARATION]
14.1 MUST NOT:
- Copy-paste components to create variants
- Introduce a second router/state/ui kit/date lib
- Bypass schemas and boundary adapters
- “Temporary hacks” that touch existing behavior directly
14.2 If tempted:
- Add an additive layer, keep old working, gate with flag, write tests.

[15. UI DESIGN SYSTEM: DARK OPS + NEON LASER (MANDATORY)]
15.1 Theme principle:
- Default UI is DARK OPS (low contrast, calm).
- NEON is accent-only. Neon MUST NOT be used as general text or large-area backgrounds.
- Neon usage is limited to:
  A) Status indication (badges)
  B) Critical alerts
  C) Primary action emphasis (very limited)
  D) Focus/selection outline

15.2 Tokens (single source of truth):
- All colors, spacing, radius, shadows MUST be defined as CSS variables in:
  src/styles/tokens.css
- Tailwind MUST reference these variables (no ad-hoc hex colors).
- Prohibited: raw hex color codes in components (except inside tokens.css).

15.3 Allowed neon accents (token names must exist):
- --accent-cyan, --accent-lime, --accent-amber, --accent-red
- --glow-soft, --glow-strong (box-shadow presets)
Rules:
- INFO uses cyan (soft glow)
- WARNING uses amber (soft glow)
- CRITICAL uses red (strong glow + pulse)
- EMERGENCY status MUST use red (strong glow)

15.4 Typography + spacing:
- 8px grid system REQUIRED (spacing scale is 4/8/12/16/24/32...).
- Use consistent hierarchy:
  - Page title: text-xl~2xl
  - Panel title: text-lg
  - Label: text-xs~sm
- Dense UI rule: No line-height smaller than readable defaults.

15.5 Layout standard (ATC control center):
- Default layout is 3-zone:
  A) Left Sidebar: list/search/filter
  B) Center Map: primary workspace
  C) Right Inspector Panel: selected entity details
- Panels MUST be resizable/collapsible only if implemented as a shared widget, not per-page hacks.

15.6 Component library rule (must be project-owned):
- Base UI primitives MUST live in:
  src/shared/ui/
- ATC-specific composites MUST live in:
  src/widgets/ (map panel, inspector, alert feed)
- Do NOT introduce another UI library. shadcn/ui pattern only.

15.7 Required components (MUST exist as shared components):
A) StatusBadge
- Variants: ONLINE, OFFLINE, DOCKED, TOWING, STOPPED, EMERGENCY, MANUAL
- Optional extended variants: EN_ROUTE, REQUESTED, APPROVED, ARRIVED
- Sizes: sm, md(default), lg
- Rules:
  - OFFLINE must look clearly disabled (no glow)
  - EMERGENCY must be visually dominant (strong glow)
  - Badge text MUST be short, uppercase, consistent.

B) AlertCard
- Levels: INFO, WARNING, CRITICAL
- CRITICAL MUST include pulse animation (subtle, not seizure-grade).
- Must include:
  - Title (type)
  - Context line (vehicleId / missionId / flightId when available)
  - Timestamp (“Just now”, “2m ago” etc.)
  - Message body
  - Optional actions (Approve/Reject) when relevant

C) NeonOutline (focus ring)
- Selected entity on map and selected list item MUST share the same focus style.
- Focus ring uses --accent-cyan unless state is CRITICAL/EMERGENCY.

15.8 Map overlay rules:
- Restricted zones MUST be shown as overlay with clear legend.
- Active route/path MUST be visually distinct from restricted zones.
- Entity label rule:
  - Vehicle/Aircraft markers MUST show a small ID label near icon.
  - Label must not overlap excessively; implement collision/priority if needed.

15.9 Motion/animation rules:
- Motion is allowed only for:
  - CRITICAL pulse
  - Loading skeletons
  - Subtle panel transitions
- Prohibited:
  - Infinite flashy animations for decoration
  - Large parallax/3D scroll gimmicks in control center

15.10 Accessibility + contrast:
- Neon accents MUST still pass readable contrast for text.
- Never use color alone to encode status: include icon/text label.
- Buttons/inputs must have visible focus state (NeonOutline).

15.11 Anti-design-drift policy:
- Any new UI element MUST reuse:
  - StatusBadge / AlertCard / shared buttons
- If a new visual pattern is needed, it MUST be added to tokens + shared/ui first.
- “Just this one page” exceptions are NOT allowed.

[16. API/REALTIME CONTRACT FREEZE & DATA SAFETY (STRICT)]
16.1 Contract Definition Location:
- API Endpoints MUST be defined only in src/shared/api/endpoints.ts (no inline strings).
- WS/MQTT Topics MUST be defined only in src/shared/realtime/topics.ts (no inline strings).

16.2 Schema Enforcement:
- Each REST response MUST have a Zod schema in src/shared/api/schemas/*.schema.ts.
- Each WS payload MUST have a Zod schema in src/shared/realtime/schemas/*.schema.ts.
- Schemas MUST match the backend API documentation exactly.

16.3 Data Types & Units:
- Coordinates: internal coordinate object is `{ x: number; y: number; headingDeg: number }`.
  - NEVER mix lat/lng with local projected x/y in the same object type.
- Units (Fixed):
  - Speed: km/h
  - Distance: meters (m)
  - Heading: degrees (0-360)
- Timestamps:
  - REST API: ISO-8601 strings (e.g. "2024-01-01T12:00:00Z").
  - WebSocket/MQTT: Epoch milliseconds (number).
  - Internal App State: Epoch milliseconds (number).

16.4 Contract Evolution:
- Any contract change MUST be additive (new optional fields, new topic, new version).
- NEVER rename or remove existing fields unless following the Breaking Change Protocol (0.5).

